{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/921226-nightmares-during-sleep-and-shape-shifting","id":921226,"title":"Nightmares during sleep, and shape shifting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-25T16:48:22-07:00","id":921226,"title":"Nightmares during sleep, and shape shifting","content":"Not to be confused, these are two separate questions.<br /> <br /> So firstly, when using a nightmare that, say, removes a target of striking looks, or effects them in a physical level, does this make people just perceive them uglier, or does it actually make then look different for the duration of the nightmare?<br /> <br /> Secondly, what's the purpose of making a nightmare trigger when a target is sleeping? Does this allow you to feed by making a dream that relates to your hunger? Do they awake with the penalties and it lasts a scene from there on out? <br /> <br /> And lastly, I would love to have a beast reminiscent to the 1982 movie monster, the thing. But there's no ativisms that allow shape shifting, and the thing was able to look like people and/or animals. Any ideas for this?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T17:01:10-07:00","id":921232,"title":"","content":"I'm reasonably certain the effects are entirely mental and/or psychosomatic.<br /> <br /> Setting Nightmares on a time delay is primarily useful for Social Maneuvering and making Chambers in a subtle fashion.<br /> <br /> Beast is just not a game thematically built for having The Thing as a PC; that's more in line with the class of being that the Rampant represent, and then only a little. Suitable Atavisms for a similar aesthetic include Infestation, From The Shadows, Monster From The Deep, plus probable others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T17:32:33-07:00","id":921245,"title":"","content":"For the sleep trigger, there's also when you want to use an effect but don't want it traced to you, like using Behold My True Form to kill someone overnight without having to touch them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}